I wrote the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses. Nothing was implemented. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored. Earlier sessions show the same pattern (only the assessment was committed, with no task files), so the files stay on disk and the implementation phase should still find them.

`task_01.md`: `/model info` shows the wrong context window (product, src/commands_info.rs)
• **Problem:** the assessment ran the real binary and got `Context: 200k tokens` for opus-5, sonnet-5, haiku-5-5, opus-4-8 and fable-5. The model presets (`anthropic_preset`) say 1M for at least opus-5 and haiku-5-5, so the display understates by 5x.
• Cause: the screen reads its own hand-kept substring table and never looks at the preset. It only affects what's displayed; the agent's real window already comes from the preset.
• Fix: use the preset's value when one exists, and keep the table only for models with no preset.
• Tests: each preset model is compared against the preset itself rather than a typed number. A non-preset model's output stays exactly as it is now. One deliberate break-and-restore check confirms the new test can fail.

`task_02.md`: `/cost` ignores Haiku 5.5's higher price for long prompts (product, src/format/cost.rs plus the cost docs)
• Problem: the Haiku 5.5 preset carries a higher rate for prompts over about 100K tokens, but nothing in cost.rs reads it. Every long prompt is priced at the base rate.
• Fix: apply the tier per request, never to the session total. The rates come from the preset, not copied numbers, and a comment states what a prompt of exactly the threshold means.
• Fallback: if no cost path can see per-request token counts, the task ships a one-line note in /cost saying the estimate uses the base rate, rather than faking it from the total.

